       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\n- **Total daily dose:** 1700 mg three times daily is 5,100 mg/day. The FDA-labeled maximum for metformin is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release, and 2,000 mg/day for extended-release in most labeling.\n- **Single dose:** 1700 mg is well above the usual maximum of about 1,000 mg per dose. A dose that high raises the risk of GI toxicity and lactic acidosis.\n\nThe 1700 may be a typo. Some possible intended orders:\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals.** This is 2,550 mg/day, the max for immediate-release.\n- **1,000 mg PO twice daily with meals.** This is 2,000 mg/day.\n- **1,700 mg total per day**, for example 850 mg PO twice daily.\n\nPlease confirm the intended dose and frequency, and whether it should be immediate-release or extended-release. Also check the plan with your resident or attending. Once you confirm, I'll enter the order right away."
      }
